~ start
While you and your army camp in the outskirts of Aşk'lan, a veiled woman suddenly approaches you. You do not know how she managed to get past your watch, in broad daylight, in her heavy attire, made for parlors, not travel. Her veil is so thick you can barely see her face; on her fingers are long fake nails of cold iron. The hem of her dusky, glittering robe is not at all dirtied, though the roads are quite dusty at this time of the year. She speaks to you, with noble, headstrong bearing, standing straight as a trellis. 

"I have come on the Behalf on the Astomancers," she begins. "It has come to our attention that you to us may be of much assistance. We do not expect you to render us this service out of sheer magnanimity; I carry a portent that may prevent your destruction. It is most unlikely that you should refuse, lest you will to part with your Life." 

~ choice

- Ask about her people
	"We are the Astromancers of Ask'lan, of course. Proprietors of Lore, Archivists of eternity, the King's dextra. The stars and beyond are the domain of our gods. It is not often that an Astromancer speaks to a land-walker like this."
	=> choice

- Ask her what "destructiòn" she speaks of
	"All shall be revealed in time," she returns. "Alpha, I await your decision. To offer assistance, or fall, a victim to hubris, not unlike so many heroes of yore."
	=> choice

- Agree to hear her out
	~ agreed
	"I am pleased with your love of reason," you can hear a smile in her voice. "It so happened that one of us had left the ivory tower some time ago and made a foray into the city below. We have not seen him since. We will you to rescue him, and cut the the Life of whomever is responsible."
	
	- Ask who captured him
		"I tell apart the stars, not kinds of land-walking trash," she sneers. "This is of no relevance, surely? I have divined his location and I am to bring you to his tormentors' very threshold. You are to penertate the premise and work your violence as you see fit."
		=> agreed
		
	- Tell her to lead you along
		$> node('DialogueIcon2').unlock()
		=> END!

- Tell her to leave
	"You shall regret this," there is suddenly a tinge of desperation in her voice. For a moment, her feigned pomp is displaced by genune emotion. "Think with that calloused heart of yours! Ere comes morn, you all shall most likely perish to a scourge from the stars! Your ignorance shall cost you dearly."
	
	- Tell her you've had it with her audacity
		=> forced_out
	
	- Force her out of the camp
		=> forced_out
		
	- Agree to let her stay and listen to her
	=> agreed
	
~ forced_out
You can hear the woman cursing in barely intelligible names as she is forced out of the camp. You cannot shake the feeling of impending doom -- was it possible that the woman's gods truly gave an omen for you? To know of an omen and yet to know not from where it would come; what could be worse? 
	
$> GameInfo.flags.append('Starwalker Omen')

=> END